msgid "Queries using metamodel attribute constants"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The query methods provided by `ManagedRepository` and `RecordRepository` can use attribute constants from the\n"
"generated Jakarta Persistence metamodel `Cat_`. These constants contain attribute names as strings; unlike the\n"
"typed attributes of `_Cat`, they do not make query parameters or expressions type-safe."
msgstr ""

msgid "String-based queries"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For queries that cannot be expressed with restrictions, use the query methods provided by `ManagedRepository` or\n"
"`RecordRepository`. These methods accept query strings, so they are not type-safe."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sorting is applied on the `BlockingDataQuery` returned by `find()` and `findAll()`, not on the shortcut `list()`,\n"
"`listAll()`, `stream()`, or `streamAll()` methods. For a single criterion, pass a `Sort` directly. Use `Order` only\n"
"when you need multiple criteria, or when receiving an `Order` from a REST endpoint:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Session and access models"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus Data Hibernate supports managed and stateless sessions with blocking and reactive APIs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Managed entities and stateful sessions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use `ManagedEntity` and `ManagedRepository` for Hibernate ORM _stateful sessions_. Entities persisted or obtained\n"
"through a stateful session are managed by Hibernate ORM, and changes to their fields are automatically sent to the\n"
"database without requiring an explicit `update` operation. The session type is `Session`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Record entities and stateless sessions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To make every update operation explicit, use a Hibernate ORM _stateless session_. Extend `RecordEntity` for the entity\n"
"and `RecordRepository` for its repository. Compared with a managed entity:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Changes to entity fields must be explicitly pushed to the database by calling `update()` on the entity or repository."
msgstr ""

msgid "Call `insert()` instead of `persist()` to insert the entity."
msgstr ""

msgid "The session type is `StatelessSession` instead of `Session`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Accessing an unfetched lazy association does not trigger automatic loading. Fetch the associations you need as part\n"
"of a repository query, using a `join fetch` clause in `@Query`. Alternatively, fetch an association explicitly with\n"
"`repo.getSession().fetch(association)`. Managed blocking sessions can load lazy associations automatically while the\n"
"session is open."
msgstr ""

msgid "Queries and the way you obtain entities remain the same. Stateless sessions can also use <<jakarta-data,Jakarta Data repositories>>."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Whether an entity is managed depends on the session used to persist or obtain it, not on its Java superclass.\n"
"For example, a `ManagedEntity` obtained through a `RecordRepository` is not managed, because that repository uses a\n"
"stateless session. See <<switching-between-managed-and-record-models,Switching between managed and record models>>\n"
"for alternative entity and repository APIs."
msgstr ""

