msgid ""
"The link:https://docs.hibernate.org/orm/{hibernate-orm-version-major-minor}/querylanguage/html_single/[Hibernate Query Language]\n"
"(HQL) is Hibernate's full query language. Hibernate ORM accepts HQL in Jakarta Data's `@Query`, including features\n"
"beyond the standard query languages."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The link:{jakarta-persistence-spec-url}#a4665[Jakarta Persistence Query Language] (JPQL) is the standard query language\n"
"defined by Jakarta Persistence and is a subset of HQL. A valid JPQL query is also a valid HQL query. This language is\n"
"evolving into the standalone link:https://jakarta.ee/specifications/query/1.0/[Jakarta Query specification]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The link:{jakarta-data-spec-url}#_jakarta_common_query_language[Jakarta Data Query Language] (JDQL) is the portable\n"
"subset of JPQL used by Jakarta Data's `@Query` annotation. Restrict queries to JDQL when the repository should remain\n"
"independent of Hibernate-specific query features."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Panache Query Language adds concise forms for common HQL queries. It is accepted by query methods such as `find()`,\n"
"`list()`, `update()`, and `delete()` on `ManagedRepository` and `RecordRepository`, and is expanded to HQL before\n"
"execution."
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid "Panache Query Language"
msgstr "Linguagem de Consulta Panache"

msgid "Most HQL select queries have the form `from EntityName [where ...] [order by ...]`, with optional elements at the end."
msgstr ""

msgid "If a select query does not start with `from`, `select`, or `with`, the following additional forms are supported:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`order by ...` expands to `from EntityName order by ...`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`<singleAttribute>` with a single parameter expands to `from EntityName where <singleAttribute> = ?`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`where <query>` expands to `from EntityName where <query>`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`<query>` expands to `from EntityName where <query>`."
msgstr ""

msgid "If an update query does not start with `update`, the following additional forms are supported:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`from EntityName ...` expands to `update EntityName ...`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`set? <singleAttribute>` with a single parameter expands to `update EntityName set <singleAttribute> = ?`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`set? <update-query>` expands to `update EntityName set <update-query>`."
msgstr ""

msgid "If a delete query does not start with `delete`, the following additional forms are supported:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`from EntityName ...` expands to `delete from EntityName ...`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`<singleAttribute>` with a single parameter expands to `delete from EntityName where <singleAttribute> = ?`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`<query>` expands to `delete from EntityName where <query>`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Repository security"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus Security provides initial support for securing repositories with security annotations. Security annotations can\n"
"be placed on methods directly declared by a repository."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can also place a security annotation on the repository interface:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Only methods directly declared on an annotated repository interface are secured. Methods inherited from\n"
"`ManagedRepository`, such as `findById`, `persist`, or `deleteAll`, are not secured because type-level annotations only\n"
"affect the type they annotate."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you need security in the repository layer, consider <<alternative-repository-definitions,plain repository classes>> that do not extend Quarkus Data ones, or roll out your own repository super interfaces, adding security annotations wherever relevant for your security model."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Generic interface methods using type variables or wildcards cannot currently be secured reliably with standard security\n"
"annotations. Apply the security annotation to the calling method, such as a REST endpoint, or redeclare the repository\n"
"method with a concrete type."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"See the xref:security-authorize-web-endpoints-reference.adoc[authorization of web endpoints reference] for information\n"
"about Quarkus Security annotations."
msgstr ""

